.TH "SIROCCO" "1" "September 2026" "Cirrus" "Cirrus Manual"
.
.SH "NAME"
\fBsirocco\fR \- A client for cirrus(1)
.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsirocco\fR [\-hv] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR\.\.] [ \. \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR\.\.] ]*
.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBsirocco\fR is the client for cirrus(1)\. It sends a given command to cirrus(1) as an X client message\. Mutation commands don\'t print anything on \fBstdout\fR\. Read\-only queries print their result on \fBstdout\fR\.
.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR
Print usage\.
.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Print version information\.
.
.TP
\fB\. (dot)\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR\.\.]
Chain sirocco command
.
.SH "COMMON DEFINITIONS"
.
.TP
\fBPOSITION\fR
topleft | topright | bottomleft | bottomright | middle
.
.TP
\fBBOOL\fR
true values: \fBtrue\fR | \fBt\fR | \fByes\fR | \fBy\fR | \fB1\fR
.
.IP
false values: \fBfalse\fR | \fBf\fR | \fBno\fR | \fBn\fR | \fB0\fR
.
.TP
\fBDIRECTION\fR
\fBup\fR | \fBdown\fR | \fBleft\fR | \fBright\fR | \fBnorth\fR | \fBsouth\fR | \fBwest\fR | \fBeast\fR
.
.TP
\fBPOINTER_ACTION\fR
\fBnothing\fR | \fBfocus\fR | \fBmove\fR | \fBresize_corner\fR | \fBresize_side\fR
.
.TP
\fBPOINTER_MODIFIER\fR
\fBalt\fR | \fBsuper\fR
.
.TP
\fBMOUSE_BUTTON\fR
\fBany\fR | \fBnone\fR | \fBleft\fR | \fBmiddle\fR | \fBcentre\fR | \fBcenter\fR | \fBright\fR
.
.IP
\fBmiddle\fR, \fBcentre\fR, and \fBcenter\fR are synonyms and have the same behaviour\.
.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.
.TP
\fBwindow move\fR \fIx\fR \fIy\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Move the selected window to the absolute position given by \fIx\fR and \fIy\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow move \-\-relative\fR \fIx\fR \fIy\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Move the selected window by the relative pixel values \fIx\fR and \fIy\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow resize\fR \fIwidth\fR \fIheight\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Resize the selected window to \fIwidth\fR and \fIheight\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow resize \-\-relative\fR \fIwidth\fR \fIheight\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Resize the selected window by the relative pixel values \fIwidth\fR and \fIheight\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow apply\-geometries\fR \fIXID\fR \fIx\fR \fIy\fR \fIwidth\fR \fIheight\fR [\.\.\.]
Apply one or more absolute geometries to explicit window IDs\. Each record has exactly five fields: \fBXID X Y WIDTH HEIGHT\fR\. All records are validated before any geometry is applied; malformed, duplicate, unknown, or unmanaged IDs cause the request to fail without applying it\. Valid records are applied in argument order and the command waits for the window manager acknowledgement\. This operation does not select targets through focus or center the pointer\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow reset\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Restore the selected window to the geometry saved by the window manager, clear its special state, restore its borders, and update \fB_NET_WM_STATE\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow maximize\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Hide the border and maximize the selected window on the current monitor\. Execute it again after maximizing to revert the state of the window\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow maximize \-\-horizontal\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Horizontally maximize the selected window on the current monitor, preserving its \fIy\fR component\. Leaves a gap at the left and right of the monitor that can be configured\. Execute it again after maximizing to revert the state of the window\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow maximize \-\-vertical\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Vertically maximize the selected window on the current monitor, preserving its \fIx\fR component\. Leaves a gap at the top and bottom of the monitor whose width can be configured\. Execute it again after maximizing to revert the state of the window\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow monocle\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Puts the selected window in the "monocled" state: full screen but with borders visible\. Monocle mode respects gaps\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow close\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Closes the selected window\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow cycle\fR
Cycle through mapped windows\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow cycle \-\-reverse\fR
Reverse cycle through mapped windows\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow cycle \-\-group\fR
Cycle through mapped windows that belong to the same group as the focused window\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow cycle \-\-group \-\-reverse\fR
Reverse cycle through mapped windows that belong to the same group as the focused window\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow focus\fR \fIwinid\fR
Focus window by \fIid\fR\. The \fIid\fR can be found using pfw(1) or lsw(1) from wmutils \fIhttps://github\.com/wmutils/core/\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow focus \-\-last\fR
Focus the window that was focused before the currently focused window\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow focus \-\-cardinal\fR \fIDIRECTION\fR
Focus the closest window in a direction, relative to the currently focused window\. Does nothing if there is no window focused\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow hide\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Hide (unmap) the selected window\. The \fIwinid\fR can be found using pfw(1) or lsw(1) from wmutils \fIhttps://github\.com/wmutils/core/\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBgroup add\fR \fIgroup_nr\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Add the selected window to the \fIgroup_nr\fR group\.
.
.IP
Group numbers start from 1 and end at \fIGROUPS_NO\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBgroup remove\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Remove the selected window from its current group\.
.
.TP
\fBgroup clear\fR \fIgroup_nr\fR
Remove all windows from the \fIgroup_nr\fR group\.
.
.TP
\fBgroup activate\fR \fIgroup_nr\fR
Map all windows that belong to the \fIgroup_nr\fR group without changing focus or stacking order\.
.
.TP
\fBgroup deactivate\fR \fIgroup_nr\fR
Unmap all windows that belong to the \fIgroup_nr\fR group without selecting a replacement focused window\.
.
.TP
\fBwm quit\fR \fIexit_status\fR
Quit cirrus with exit_status \fIexit_status\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBwm config\fR \fIkey\fR [\fIvalues\fR\.\.\.]
See \fICONFIGURING\fR\.
.
.SH "QUERYING"
.
.TP
\fBwindow focused\fR
Print the currently focused managed window ID in \fB0x%08x\fR format\. If no managed window is focused, print an error and exit with a nonzero status\. The query also exits nonzero if cirrus does not respond within two seconds\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow ids\fR [\-\-all] [\fIclassname\fR] [\-\-name \fIname\fR]
Print managed window IDs, one per line\. Without \fB\-\-all\fR, only mapped windows are included; \fB\-\-all\fR includes all managed windows\. An optional classname or name restricts the result\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow count\fR [\-\-all] [\fIclassname\fR] [\-\-name \fIname\fR]
Print the number of windows selected by the same collection options as \fBwindow ids\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow classname\fR
Print the focused managed window\'s class name\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow stack\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Print the connected transitive overlap cluster containing the selected window, one window ID per line in actual X stacking order from bottom to top\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow stack\-geometries\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Print the connected transitive overlap cluster containing the selected window, one record per line in stack order\. Each record is \fBXID X Y WIDTH HEIGHT\fR, using the same geometry convention as \fBwindow geometry\fR\. Membership and geometry are captured by one window\-manager query\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow geometry\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Print the selected managed window\'s geometry as \fBX=\fR, \fBY=\fR, \fBWIDTH=\fR, and \fBHEIGHT=\fR records\. An explicit ID is addressed directly; without one, the focused managed window is selected\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow group\fR \fIwinid\fR
Print the public one\-based group number for the explicit managed window ID\. Prints \fB4294967295\fR when the window has no group\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow groups \-\-all\fR
Print every managed window and its public one\-based group as \fBXID GROUP\fR, including unmapped windows\. \fB4294967295\fR denotes the null group\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow snapshot\fR
Print the normalized version\-1 managed\-window snapshot:
.
.IP "" 4
.
.nf

  SNAPSHOT 1
  FOCUSED XID|NONE
  CURRENT GROUP|4294967295
  CLIENT XID GROUP MAPPED
.
.fi
.
.IP "" 0
.
.IP
Groups are public one\-based values\. \fBMAPPED\fR is \fB0\fR or \fB1\fR, and \fB4294967295\fR is the null\-group sentinel\. This is a read\-only observation\.
.
.TP
\fBwindow stack cycle\fR [\fIwinid\fR]
Focus and raise the selected window if it is not already the topmost member of its canonical stack\. If it is topmost, focus and raise the bottommost member\. A single\-member stack is left unchanged\.
.
.P
Information about the current state of cirrus is available through X properties of the root window\. Example:
.
.IP "" 4
.
.nf

xprop \-root CIRRUS_ACTIVE_GROUPS
.
.fi
.
.IP "" 0
.
.P
Information about the current state of each managed window is available through X properties of the window\. Example:
.
.IP "" 4
.
.nf

xprop \-id 0x02c00009 CIRRUS_STATUS
.
.fi
.
.IP "" 0
.
.P
Here is a list of exposed properties:
.
.TP
\fBCIRRUS_ACTIVE_GROUPS\fR
On the root window\. An integer list of currently active groups\.
.
.TP
\fBCIRRUS_STATUS\fR
On each managed window\. Contains information about the window\. Notable properties: \fBgroup\fR is \-1 if the window is not in a group\. \fBstate\fR can have one of the following values: \fBnormal\fR, \fBmaxed\fR, \fBvmaxed\fR, \fBhmaxed\fR, \fBmonocled\fR\.
.
.SH "CONFIGURING"
Configuring is done using the \fBwm config\fR command\. Possible configuration keys are:
.
.TP
\fBouter_border_width\fR \fIwidth\fR
Sets the outer border width to \fIwidth\fR pixels\.
.
.TP
\fBouter_color_focused\fR, \fBouter_color_unfocused\fR \fIouter_color\fR
Sets the outer border color to \fIouter_color\fR for the focused and unfocused state respectively\. \fIouter_color\fR is a hexadecimal value that may or may not start with \fB0x\fR prefix\. Example: \fB0x1234ef\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBinner_border_width\fR \fIwidth\fR
Make the first \fIwidth\fR pixels from the interior to the exterior of the inner border use another color, so you get inner and outer borders\. The width of the outer border is \fBouter_border_width \- inner_border_width\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBinner_color_focused\fR, \fBinner_color_unfocused\fR \fIinner_color\fR
Like \fBouter_color_focused\fR and \fBouter_color_unfocused\fR, but for the inner border\. \fIinner_color\fR uses the same hexadecimal format as \fIouter_color\fR\.
.
.P
The legacy \fBborder_width\fR, \fBcolor_focused\fR, \fBcolor_unfocused\fR, \fBinternal_border_width\fR, \fBinternal_color_focused\fR, and \fBinternal_color_unfocused\fR configuration keys remain accepted with the same arguments and behavior\.
.
.TP
\fBgap_width\fR \fIPOSITION\fR \fIwidth\fR
Sets the window gap at \fIPOSITION\fR to \fIwidth\fR\. \fIPOSITION\fR can be equal to \fBall\fR to set all gaps to \fIPOSITION\fR\.
.
.TP
\fBcursor_position\fR \fIPOSITION\fR
Sets the position of the cursor when moving or resizing windows\.
.
.TP
\fBgroups_nr\fR \fInr\fR
Sets the number of groups to \fInr\fR\. If \fInr\fR is less than the current number of groups, window that belong to groups whose numbers are greater than \fInr\fR will be mapped to screen and assigned to the null group\.
.
.TP
\fBenable_resize_hints\fR \fIBOOL\fR
If true, \fBcirrus\fR will respect window resize hints as defined by ICCCM\. Most terminal emulators should have this feature\.
.
.TP
\fBenable_sloppy_focus\fR \fIBOOL\fR
Enable sloppy focus\.
.
.TP
\fBsticky_windows\fR \fIBOOL\fR
If \fIsticky_windows\fR is true, new windows will be assigned to the last activated group automatically\. Recommended for people who like using workspaces over groups\.
.
.TP
\fBenable_borders\fR \fIBOOL\fR
If true, the border will be fully managed by the window manager\. Border colors will be set each time a window gets/loses focus\. Setting it to false lets the user manage the border of every window using external tools\. (example: \fBchwb2\fR from wmutils)\.
.
.TP
\fBenable_last_window_focusing\fR \fIBOOL\fR
If true, when the currently focused window is unmapped or closed, \fBcirrus\fR will focus the previously focused window\. See the \fBwindow focus \-\-last\fR command\.
.
.TP
\fBapply_settings\fR \fIBOOL\fR
If true, some settings will be applied on all windows instead of newly created windows\. True by default\.
.
.TP
\fBreplay_click_on_focus\fR \fIBOOL\fR
If true, when clicking on an unfocused with the intent to focus it, cirrus will also send the click event to the target window\. If false, the window will receive the click event only if it\'s already focused\.
.
.TP
\fBpointer_actions\fR \fIPOINTER_ACTION\fR \fIPOINTER_ACTION\fR \fIPOINTER_ACTION\fR
Sets the action that should be done whenever the modifier key and the corresponding button are clicked at the same time on the window\. There are 3 actions for three mouse buttons: left, middle and right\.
.
.TP
\fBpointer_modifier\fR \fIPOINTER_MODIFIER\fR
Set the modifier for pointer actions\.
.
.TP
\fBclick_to_focus\fR \fIMOUSE_BUTTON\fR
Set the mouse button that focuses the hovered window when clicked\.
.
